# Website Meeting live session

Authority: `docs/platforms/website/organization-host-routing.md` §5.3.
Transport / `connect_error`: `.cursor/rules/meeting-realtime-socket.mdc`.

## Public surface

- Layout mounts **`MeetingLiveProvider` → `MeetingLiveSessionProvider` → shell**.
- Product UI consumes **`useMeetingLiveSession()`** (context reader) → `{ linking, can, actions, meeting, me, attendWindow }`.
- Pure `resolveMeetingLiveSession` lives **in the same file** as the provider/hook: `hooks/useMeetingLiveSession.tsx`. Pure resolve returns **`MeetingLiveSessionState`** (`linking` + `can` only). Instance adds `actions`, `meeting`, `me`, `attendWindow` **once** for the tree.
- Attend-window clock lives in `hooks/useMeetingAttendWindow.ts` — called **once** from the session instance; screens read `attendWindow` (do not call the hook again). Mirror math stays private.
- `MeetingLiveLinking` = `"PENDING" | "READY" | "FAILED"` — the **only** derived session enum. Do not reintroduce remapped meeting/me stage enums.
- Do **not** reintroduce a nested `stages` object, re-resolve session in every screen, or fold session into `MeetingLiveProvider`.
- Keep `useMeetingLive()` for raw transport flags and for `batch` when **implementing** a new action. Do not re-derive linking or action gates in screens.

## Write contract

- `meeting` / `me` on session are **read** proxies for product UI — do not assign fields from screens.
- Product writes go **only** through `actions.*` (each checks `can.*`, then uses `batch` internally).
- Do **not** put `batch` on the session return value. New collaborative writes = new `actions` + `can` entry.

## Linking

| Value | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `PENDING` | Not ready, no session `error` (includes transport-only reconnect) |
| `READY` | `connected && synced`, no error |
| `FAILED` | `error != null` |

When `linking !== "READY"`: every `can.*` is false. Session value still includes `meeting` / `me` / `attendWindow`; shell does not mount product chrome.

`MeetingShell` must show **only** `MeetingLinkingScreen` until READY — no header/drawer/footer/page children. READY shell drawer/header IA: `.cursor/rules/website-meeting-shell.mdc`.

## Gate UI patterns

- MeetingLinkingScreen reads `linking` from `useMeetingLiveSession()` — no `linking` prop from the layout.
- PENDING loading: project **`Loadable`** — never invent a custom spinner.
- FAILED: shared `LaneFailed` (`components/Wrong`) inside a `relative` page-background wrapper — no hand-rolled icon + message.
- Org identity: show **logo and name when both exist** (not XOR).
- Copy under `ui.layouts.meetingLayout.linking` (ar + en).

## Actions

| Action | When `can.*` |
|---|---|
| `startMeeting` | `emitLiveStart()` then `batch` → `meeting.status = "STARTED"` |
| `endMeeting` | `batch` → `meeting.status = "COMPLETED"` then `emitLiveComplete()` |
| `attend` | `me.attendedAt = ISO` |
| `left` | `me.leftAt = ISO` |
| `setAgendaItemStatus(id, status)` | `meeting.agendaItems[id].status = status` (no-op if missing item) |
| `raiseHand` | `me.talkTurn = nextTalkTurn(participants)` |
| `lowerHand` | `me.talkTurn = null` |
| `giveTalkFloor` | `meeting.currentTalkMemberId = head.id` **and** `head.talkTurn = null` (head from `findQueueHead`; no argument) |
| `removeFromTalkQueue(memberId)` | `participants[memberId].talkTurn = null` (no-op if missing or not queued) |
| `endTalkFloor` | `meeting.currentTalkMemberId = null` |
| `castVote(decisionId, value)` | `decisions[id].votes[meId] = { memberId, value, castAt }` — open ballot, phase `cast` gate, never overwrites an existing cast |
| `setDecisionStatus(decisionId, status, votingType?)` | open (`DURING` + `NEW` + `votingType` + no other open DURING row) or settle (`ACCEPTED`/`REJECTED` on strict majority, `CANCELED` always) — phase `manage` gate |
| `clearDecisionVotes(decisionId)` | empties `decisions[id].votes` on an open ballot — phase `manage` gate |

- Sync; no-op when `!can.*` (and `attend`/`left`/`raiseHand`/`lowerHand` require `me`).
- Lifecycle emits come from `useMeetingLive()` (`emitLiveStart` / `emitLiveComplete`); session must not invent a second socket. No `meeting.live.completed` listener for status.
- Product UI for `endMeeting`: Meeting info (`init`) only, behind `confirm(..., "danger")`. Do not add a second end surface on broadcast.
- `can.enterLive` is a **navigation + LiveKit token gate** (no matching action write): true when `attendedAt` set and `leftAt` unset. `useMeetingLiveKitToken` requires `can.enterLive` **before** `STARTED` / route ids.
- `can.muteAllMedia` is a **UI gate only** for the chair mute-all controls in `MeetingLiveBroadcast` (chair + `STARTED`); the commands travel on the LiveKit data channel, not `actions`.
- `can.setAgendaItemStatus` is chair + meeting live (`WAITING_TO_START` \| `STARTED`). Live-map `status` only until complete reflect. Active line = `DISCUSSING` (no root pointer).
- Talk-queue gates: `raiseHand` / `lowerHand` are **non-chair** + `enterLive` + meeting live (`raiseHand` also needs `talkTurn == null` and `meId !== currentTalkMemberId`); `giveTalkFloor` / `removeFromTalkQueue` / `endTalkFloor` are chair + meeting live (`giveTalkFloor` needs a queue head, `endTalkFloor` needs a floor holder). Live-map `talkTurn` / `currentTalkMemberId` only — **no** SQL `TalkRecord`. Order and display rules: `.cursor/rules/meeting-talk-queue.mdc`.
- Decision gates are **phase-explicit**: `castPreStartVote` / `castDuringVote` (voter) and `managePreStartDecision` / `manageDuringDecision` (chair); pre-start = meeting live, during = `enterLive` + `STARTED`. Actions and `useMeetingDecisions` map a decision to its pair through the exported `decisionPhaseCan(can, phase)` — never hand-pick a key. `countDecisionVotes` is exported for the same reason. Ballot rules: `.cursor/rules/meeting-decisions-vote.mdc`.
- `can.attend` also requires `attendWindow.windowOpen` (mirror of `MeetingModel.ATTEND_OPEN_BEFORE_MS` private to `useMeetingAttendWindow`) and, for voters, `preStartVotesComplete` (computed once in the instance and passed into resolve).
- Session provider calls `useMeetingAttendWindow(meeting.datetime)` once, passes `windowOpen` into resolve, and exposes `attendWindow` on the session value.
- Client `can` gates are **not** full server authz — CRDT updates still use `MEETING_LIVE_STATUSES`; chair **lifecycle** start/complete are server-enforced (`NOT_CHAIR`). Attend-window / ordinary CRDT participant-type / ballot invariants are not fully socket-enforced.
- Init remaining-duration copy reads `attendWindow` from session — do not call `useMeetingAttendWindow` again in the page.

## Forbidden

- Calling `useMeetingAttendWindow` from product pages/shell (second clock).
- Reintroducing loose `meeting/meetingAttendWindow.ts` or `meeting/meetingLiveSession.ts` at the meeting root.
- Exporting attend-window mirror predicates/constants from the hook module.
- Putting navigation (`setPage`) inside attendance/session data hooks.
